---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About" description="Austin Wakefield — background, AI philosophy, and what I'm looking for.">
  <section class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">About</h1>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Background</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--text-dim)]">
      I'm currently a Shift Lead at Jersey Mike's — about three years in that role — while studying web development.
      I've been around computers most of my life, and the idea of building something real inside one, from nothing,
      is what actually pulled me into programming. My foundation is in Python, and I'm early in my career: I'd
      rather be straightforward about that than dress it up.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-white">How I use AI</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--text-dim)]">
      I think of myself as the one directing the tools, not the one being replaced by them. I use Claude, Claude
      Code, ChatGPT, and Perplexity to move faster — to understand concepts, explore approaches, debug, and improve
      code — but the thinking, the decisions, and the parts that need hand-written code stay mine. Both projects on
      this site were built that way, and the <a href="/ai-workflow" class="text-[var(--accent-2)]">AI Workflow page</a>{" "}
      shows the actual decisions and mistakes behind them, not just a summary.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Faith</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--text-dim)]">
      My faith is the center of who I am, and it shapes how I show up at work — with patience, honesty, and the
      belief that how I treat people matters as much as what I build. If there's one thing I'd want you to know
      about me beyond the code, it's that.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-white">What I'm looking for</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--text-dim)]">
      A team that communicates clearly and works at a pace that respects that people have a life outside of work —
      church, school, friends, rest. I bring curiosity, patience, and a real willingness to keep learning; in
      return, I'm looking for a team that won't run me into the ground.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
